From 8876d77dd27ef9afea41193fae85857c5c83f590 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bill Hlavacek <hlavacek@lanl.gov>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 11:16:01 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] bngsim: read mu::Parser literals as strtod does via host
 expr_compat

ExprTk's own number parser is not correctly rounded: it sums digits in
a double and scales by a power of ten, so 7.77e-05 read as
7.769999999999999e-05 and 0.49999999999999997 as 0.5, where muParser,
strtod and the host evaluator's generated C read the correctly rounded
double. Pass the remapped expression through the host single source
bngsim::expr_compat::exact_literals, which respells only the literals
ExprTk would misread, the same way the host evaluator now compiles.
(bngsim issue #1013)
---
 src/NFfunction/nfsim_funcparser.h | 6 ++++--
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/NFfunction/nfsim_funcparser.h b/src/NFfunction/nfsim_funcparser.h
index 85831f9..be019fb 100644
--- a/src/NFfunction/nfsim_funcparser.h
+++ b/src/NFfunction/nfsim_funcparser.h
@@ -294,8 +294,10 @@ private:
 
     void compile() {
         // Recompute the remapped expression from the original each time so that
-        // any symbol registered before this (re)compile is reflected.
-        expr_string_ = remapExpression(original_expr_string_);
+        // any symbol registered before this (re)compile is reflected. Then
+        // respell any literal ExprTk's own number parser would misread, so it
+        // reads as strtod (and the host evaluator) reads it.
+        expr_string_ = bngsim::expr_compat::exact_literals(remapExpression(original_expr_string_));
 
         expression_ = exprtk::expression<double>();  // reset
         expression_.register_symbol_table(symbol_table_);
